From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 05:08:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] dosboot: accept nobootrequesters argument

AmigaOS system volumes can need to start before the disk-installed AROS GUI
libraries exist.  Expose the existing BF_NO_BOOT_REQUESTERS policy as a boot
argument so the initial CLI can run over NIL: without starting CON and its GUI
library lookups.  The flag already carries through CliInit and __dos_Boot.
---
 rom/dosboot/dosboot_init.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rom/dosboot/dosboot_init.c b/rom/dosboot/dosboot_init.c
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/rom/dosboot/dosboot_init.c
+++ b/rom/dosboot/dosboot_init.c
@@ -196,6 +196,10 @@ int dosboot_Init(LIBBASETYPEPTR LIBBASE)
                     LIBBASE->db_BootFlags |= BF_EMERGENCY_CONSOLE;
                     D(bug("[DOSBoot] %s: Emergency console selected\n", __func__));
                 }
+                else if (0 == stricmp(node->ln_Name, "nobootrequesters"))
+                {
+                    LIBBASE->db_BootFlags |= BF_NO_BOOT_REQUESTERS;
+                }
             }
             IntExpBase(ExpansionBase)->BootFlags = LIBBASE->db_BootFlags;
         }
-- 
